# Supply-chain policy, matching the sibling metalabel repos.
#   - minimum-release-age: a third-party publish must be 7 days old (10080
#     minutes) before we can resolve it, so a compromised release has time to
#     be caught and yanked. `pnpm update` will therefore pick the newest
#     version older than that window, not always "latest".
#   - trust-policy=no-downgrade: refuse a version whose provenance is weaker
#     than a version we already resolved. Investigate the package when this
#     fires; never bypass it with `--config.trust-policy=accept`.
#   - block-exotic-subdeps: no transitive git/URL/tarball dependencies.
#   - strict peers and strict engines: unmet peers and wrong Node fail loudly.
strict-peer-dependencies=true
engine-strict=true
minimum-release-age=10080
trust-policy=no-downgrade
block-exotic-subdeps=true

# First-party: published from the metalabel/dfos repo, pinned exact here as a
# devDependency and adopted the same day it is released, so the third-party
# 7-day quarantine does not apply. `dfos-protocol` and `dfos-web-relay` are the
# same release train and are `dfos-client`'s peers, so they must be resolvable
# on the same day or the peer graph cannot close.
minimum-release-age-exclude[]=@metalabel/dfos-client
minimum-release-age-exclude[]=@metalabel/dfos-protocol
minimum-release-age-exclude[]=@metalabel/dfos-web-relay
